From: ouroboros420 <ouroboros420@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] plugin: keep forking plugin processes on Python 3.14

Plugin processes are started with multiprocessing's default start method and
inherit the sandboxed plugin object and its socket. Python 3.14 changed the
Linux default from fork to forkserver, which would try to pickle them. The
release binaries bundle an older Python, so this only shows up when the
loader runs on a 3.14 system interpreter. Ask for the fork context
explicitly.
---
--- a/decky_loader/plugin/plugin.py
+++ b/decky_loader/plugin/plugin.py
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 from json import dumps, load, loads
 from logging import getLogger
 from os import path
-from multiprocessing import Process
+from multiprocessing import Process, get_context
 from time import time
 from traceback import format_exc
 
@@ -139,7 +139,8 @@
     def start(self):
         if self.passive:
             return self
-        self.proc = Process(target=self.sandboxed_plugin.initialize, args=[self._socket])
+        # Plugins inherit the sandbox and its socket; Python 3.14 defaults to forkserver.
+        self.proc = get_context("fork").Process(target=self.sandboxed_plugin.initialize, args=[self._socket])
         self.proc.start()
         self._listener_task = create_task(self._response_listener())
         return self
